    "gradeBand": "4",
    "overview": "Divide with place value strategies and decide what a remainder means in a story.",
    "problems": [
      {
        "prompt": "Find 96 ÷ 4 by breaking 96 into 80 and 16."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Find 158 ÷ 6. Write the quotient and the remainder."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Find 1,236 ÷ 3. Check your answer with multiplication."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "75 students are going on a field trip. Each van holds 8 students. How many vans are needed? Explain what you did with the remainder."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A ribbon is 50 inches long. It is cut into pieces that are 6 inches long. How many full pieces are there? How much ribbon is left over?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "4 friends share 30 baseball cards equally. How many cards does each friend get? How many are left over?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "A library has 6 shelves with 124 books on each shelf. It gives away 94 books, then packs the rest into boxes that hold 9 books each. How many boxes does it need? Estimate first to check that your answer is reasonable."
      }
    ],
